# opencode-goku-team

OpenCode plugin that injects a `goku` primary orchestrator agent and four subagents: `explore`, `planner`, `developer`, and `reviewer`.

By default, the plugin also injects a local MCP server named `codegraph` unless `cfg.mcp.codegraph` is already defined elsewhere in your opencode config.

## Installation

Install and reference it from `opencode.json` through the `plugin` array.

The default MCP integration requires a `codegraph` executable on your `PATH`. Install the `codegraph` CLI before relying on the default `codegraph serve --mcp` command.

As an npm package:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    "opencode-goku-team"
  ]
}
```

If you want to pass plugin options, use the tuple form:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "agents": {
          "goku": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "medium" }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

As a local plugin from `~/.config/opencode/plugin/goku/index.ts`, reference it from `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    "./plugin/goku/index.ts"
  ]
}
```

Or with options:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "./plugin/goku/index.ts",
      {
        "agents": {
          "goku": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "medium" }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

## What It Provides

The plugin injects five agents into opencode:

- `goku`: the primary orchestrator agent. This is the default agent unless you override `defaultAgent`.
- `explore`: codebase exploration and context gathering.
- `planner`: planning and task breakdown.
- `developer`: implementation and debugging.
- `reviewer`: review for bugs, regressions, and missing coverage.

## Configuration

OpenCode config does not allow unknown top-level fields, so this plugin must be configured through plugin options inside the `plugin` array.

### Default behavior

No options are required. The plugin injects all five agents, sets the default agent to `goku`, and adds a default local `codegraph` MCP server when `cfg.mcp.codegraph` is not already present.

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    "opencode-goku-team"
  ]
}
```

The injected MCP entry is:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "codegraph": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["codegraph", "serve", "--mcp"],
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

If you already define `mcp.codegraph` in `opencode.json`, the plugin leaves that entry untouched.

### Disable the default `codegraph` MCP integration

Use `false` when you want the plugin to write an explicit disabled entry instead of the default local server:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "codegraph": false
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

This form is also accepted:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "codegraph": { "enabled": false }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

### Customize the injected `codegraph` MCP server

When you want the plugin to manage the server but override the default launch details, use the schema-safe `command`, `cwd`, `timeout`, and `environment` keys:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "codegraph": {
          "command": ["codegraph", "serve", "--mcp", "--stdio"],
          "cwd": "~/src/my-monorepo",
          "timeout": 15000,
          "environment": {
            "CODEGRAPH_CACHE_DIR": "~/.cache/codegraph"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

Unknown `codegraph` option keys are ignored so the plugin only writes fields that match opencode's config schema.

### Set the `goku` primary agent's model and variant

Use the `agents` form when you want explicit per-agent configuration.

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "agents": {
          "goku": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "medium" }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

### Configure each subagent's model and variant

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "agents": {
          "goku": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "medium" },
          "explore": { "model": "opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash", "variant": "medium" },
          "planner": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "variant": "xhigh" },
          "developer": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "high" },
          "reviewer": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.5", "variant": "xhigh" }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

### Use the `models` and `variants` shorthand

The shorthand form is equivalent, but split across two maps.

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "models": {
          "goku": "openai/gpt-5.4",
          "explore": "opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash",
          "planner": "openai/gpt-5.5",
          "developer": "openai/gpt-5.4",
          "reviewer": "openai/gpt-5.5"
        },
        "variants": {
          "goku": "medium",
          "explore": "medium",
          "planner": "xhigh",
          "developer": "high",
          "reviewer": "xhigh"
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

### Change the default agent via `defaultAgent`

By default, the plugin sets opencode's `default_agent` to `goku`. Override that with `defaultAgent` if you want a different starting agent.

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "defaultAgent": "developer",
        "agents": {
          "goku": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "medium" },
          "developer": { "model": "openai/gpt-5.4", "variant": "high" }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

### Compatibility wrapper

For compatibility, the plugin also accepts the same options wrapped in a `goku` key:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-goku-team",
      {
        "goku": {
          "defaultAgent": "developer",
          "models": {
            "goku": "openai/gpt-5.4",
            "developer": "openai/gpt-5.4"
          },
          "variants": {
            "goku": "medium",
            "developer": "high"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

## Options Reference

```ts
type Options = {
  defaultAgent?: string
  agents?: Record<string, { model?: string; variant?: string }>
  models?: Record<string, string>
  variants?: Record<string, string>
  codegraph?:
    | false
    | {
        enabled?: boolean
        command?: string[]
        cwd?: string
        timeout?: number
        environment?: Record<string, string>
      }
}
```

- `defaultAgent?: string`: sets opencode's `default_agent`. Defaults to `"goku"` when omitted.
- `agents?: Record<string, { model?: string; variant?: string }>`: explicit per-agent overrides. Valid keys are `goku`, `explore`, `planner`, `developer`, and `reviewer`.
- `models?: Record<string, string>`: shorthand model overrides by agent name.
- `variants?: Record<string, string>`: shorthand variant overrides by agent name.
- `codegraph?: false | { enabled?: boolean; command?: string[]; cwd?: string; timeout?: number; environment?: Record<string, string> }`: controls the plugin-managed `mcp.codegraph` entry. The plugin preserves any existing `cfg.mcp.codegraph`; otherwise it injects the default local server or an explicit disabled entry.

If both forms are present for the same agent, `agents[agentName].model` and `agents[agentName].variant` take precedence over `models[agentName]` and `variants[agentName]`.

For compatibility, wrapping these options in a top-level `goku` key is also accepted, but the direct form is preferred.

## Agent Templates

Agent definitions live in `agents/*.md`. Each file uses opencode-style frontmatter plus a markdown prompt body. The plugin reads these files at startup and injects them into `cfg.agent`.

## Important Notes

- opencode config must be passed as plugin options. Do not add unknown top-level fields to `opencode.json`.
- Restart opencode after changing plugin config, this plugin, or any agent template.
- The plugin reads `agents/*.md` at startup, so template changes are only picked up on the next restart.
- The `codegraph` MCP integration is also loaded from config at startup, so option changes require a full opencode restart.
